@clawsweeper re-review

Please review current head `056529ed65769bfdfe6d1f6adac7dcf6f3c25644`. It incorporates main’s merged routing repair and removes our duplicate entry; CI had rejected only the combined merge tree containing both. All 25 other PR files are unchanged, the six rebased commits are patch-identical, and the post-rebase completion/registry checks pass 27/27. The selected-owner planner now yields 80 rows within the existing 130-row cap, with one hot-reload owner and no duplicate database registry entries.

The verified Doctor mock-export repair and non-streamed attachment proof remain intact. The separate standalone Doctor cold-start risk is explicitly documented in the PR and #160383, not claimed resolved. Review only; no autofix or merge is requested.
